WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:03.875
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Hello.

2
00:00:04.041 --> 00:00:09.406
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Good evening, sir, madam. What would you like to drink?

3
00:00:09.738 --> 00:00:11.907
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Do you have champagne?

4
00:00:12.073 --> 00:00:13.199
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Yes, sir.

5
00:00:13.298 --> 00:00:15.931
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Two glasses of champagne, please.

6
00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.208
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Here you are!

7
00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:25.023
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Cheers, Kim.

8
00:00:25.536 --> 00:00:29.064
<v><b>Kim:</b></v> Cheers. To our new house.

9
00:00:29.726 --> 00:00:31.962
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> You’re Americans, aren’t you?

10
00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:35.903
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Yes, that’s right. We’re from California.

11
00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:40.292
<v><b>Kim:</b></v> But this afternoon we rented the big house near here.

12
00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:44.995
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Which house? The Travers family’s house?

13
00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.254
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Yes.

14
00:00:47.032 --> 00:00:48.042
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Oh.

15
00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:50.096
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Is something wrong?

16
00:00:50.328 --> 00:00:52.530
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Who showed you the house?

17
00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:57.151
<v><b>Kim:</b></v> Barbara. The old lady who lived there before.

18
00:00:57.316 --> 00:01:03.361
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Ahh. Barbara. Old Mr Travers’ daughter.

19
00:01:04.056 --> 00:01:07.451
Some people thought that she was the one that did it.

20
00:01:08.014 --> 00:01:11.823
<v><b>Kim:</b></v> The one that did what? What happened?

21
00:01:12.121 --> 00:01:13.678
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Didn’t she tell you?

22
00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:15.351
<v><b>Kim:</b></v> Tell us what?

23
00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.735
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> About the murder.

24
00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.541
<v><b>Leo &amp; Kim:</b></v> Murder?

25
00:01:19.673 --> 00:01:28.765
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Yes, Mr Travers was murdered in that house in 1965…in his bed.

26
00:01:29.576 --> 00:01:31.514
<v><b>Kim:</b></v> Oh, how horrible!

27
00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:36.035
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> The man who killed Mr Travers was Barbara’s lover.

28
00:01:36.532 --> 00:01:38.933
The family never lived there again.

29
00:01:39.364 --> 00:01:44.580
They tried to sell the house, but nobody wanted to buy it.

30
00:01:45.325 --> 00:01:51.618
Not after a murder. That’s why that house is always rented.

31
00:01:52.264 --> 00:01:55.196
Barbara never married, of course.

32
00:01:55.643 --> 00:01:56.537
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Kim?

33
00:01:56.703 --> 00:01:57.647
<v><b>Kim:</b></v> Yes?

34
00:01:57.829 --> 00:02:00.197
<v><b>Leo:</b></v> Are you thinking what I’m thinking?

35
00:02:00.379 --> 00:02:05.099
<v><b>Kim:</b></v> Yes – I don’t want to live in a house where somebody was murdered.

36
00:02:05.438 --> 00:02:07.078
Come on. Let’s go.

37
00:02:07.094 --> 00:02:11.723
<v><b>Barman:</b></v> Hey, hey, your champagne! You didn’t drink your champagne…

38
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.124
Ah, well.